        <obo:IAO_0000115>Core histone that, along with other histones, forms the nucleosome, a fundamental unit of chromatin. Plays a crucial role in transcription regulation. Histone H3 is subject to various post-translational modifications, including acetylation, methylation, phosphorylation, and ubiquitination that influence chromatin structure and gene expression.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>pubmed:37220590</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
