        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A role played by a chemical agent which exhibits the capability of occupying space between DNA base pairs due to particular properties in size, shape and charge. Intercalation of chemical compounds in DNA helix can result in replication errors (shift, mutation) or DNA damages.</obo:IAO_0000115>
